<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech PSE closed for May 1 holiday.</title>
<headline>Czech PSE closed for May 1 holiday.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Prague Stock Exchange was closed on Thursday as the country celebrates the May 1 holiday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the PSE's PX50 index fell, led down by losses to shares in banks IPB and Komercni, and dealers said the market could go still lower on Friday after the holiday.</p>
<p>The PX50 fell two points, or 0.38 percent, to 529.3.</p>
</text>
